  "structure": "45 EC first-year required + 85 EC major + 10 EC electives + 30 EC for minor, study abroad or electives + 10 EC Global Citizenship. Three first-year choices total 15 EC, one of which counts toward a further graduation requirement. The displayed seven compulsory components sum to 45 EC. Mathematics for Social Networks is one allowed maths choice. The older upper-year example uses 15 EC foundations, 15 EC methods, 45 EC choices including four level-300 modules, and 10 EC capstone. The class of 2028 example moves 5 EC from choices to the capstone. No module or handbook confirmed the complete 2029 allocation.",
  "neutralSelection": "CHS is the broad humanities and social science expression of the generic degree. Its compulsory culture, history and social theory courses make the breadth identifiable before looking at UCR. The six formal majors in the annual guide include GHIS. There is no stable health generator in these 33 target rows.",
